[SPEAKER_02]: Have that view, have that experience of a higher self, a higher form of self that seems to be unchanged by these more kind of perturbing changes that happen on the level of this kind of temporal self here and now.

13
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,102
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can't just stop having that view.

14
00:02:18,342 --> 00:02:19,102
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, why would you?

15
00:02:21,064 --> 00:02:23,046
[SPEAKER_02]: But how can you how can you overcome that view?

16
00:02:23,926 --> 00:02:26,649
[SPEAKER_02]: So, how can you overcome view of a higher self that does factually

17
00:02:27,755 --> 00:02:29,636
[SPEAKER_02]: It helps you cope with life much better.

18
00:02:31,737 --> 00:02:34,438
[SPEAKER_02]: Helps you not be perturbed as much.

19
00:02:34,818 --> 00:02:40,301
[SPEAKER_02]: When this this kind of lower self gets affected, this higher self gives you perspective.

20
00:02:41,282 --> 00:02:46,204
[SPEAKER_02]: So, eh... Well, let's say, first of all, what's the problem?

21
00:02:46,684 --> 00:02:47,645
[SPEAKER_02]: What's the problem with that?

22
00:02:48,025 --> 00:02:48,805
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is that a problem?

23
00:02:49,926 --> 00:02:51,467
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is the Advaita view a problem?

24
00:02:52,367 --> 00:02:54,468
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, this is... Why is the higher self an issue?

25
00:02:54,548 --> 00:02:57,869
[SPEAKER_01]: It's turning consciousness into a thing.

26
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,230
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I don't know anything about that.

27
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:00,990
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know.

28
00:03:01,031 --> 00:03:02,251
[SPEAKER_02]: I never heard the word consciousness.

29
00:03:02,671 --> 00:03:03,251
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know anything.

30
00:03:03,311 --> 00:03:06,933
[SPEAKER_02]: I just know that having a higher sense of self makes my life better.

31
00:03:07,253 --> 00:03:10,174
[SPEAKER_02]: What's the problem with it, practically speaking?

32
00:03:10,494 --> 00:03:11,735
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there an issue with that?

33
00:03:11,835 --> 00:03:14,576
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is it an issue to have a higher self as a reference point?

34
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:25,469
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I mean, yeah, I mean, ultimately, it's because you can't discern with this, this is.

35
00:03:25,649 --> 00:03:26,369
[SPEAKER_01]: Paticca Saṃphāda.

36
00:03:26,489 --> 00:03:27,009
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't care.

37
00:03:27,189 --> 00:03:27,369
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

38
00:03:27,549 --> 00:03:32,371
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't need to, because I'm, again, higher sense of self frees me from suffering here and now.

39
00:03:32,612 --> 00:03:32,832
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

40
00:03:32,992 --> 00:03:36,573
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't need, I don't know what you're talking about, this, that, Paticca Saṃphāda.

41
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:42,095
[SPEAKER_02]: Factually, when I'm devoted to the higher Atman or something, I have no pain.

42
00:03:43,456 --> 00:03:44,096
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the problem?

43
00:03:44,716 --> 00:03:45,657
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm free from suffering.

44
00:03:45,677 --> 00:03:47,498
[SPEAKER_02]: Isn't that what you, isn't that what the Buddha teaches

45
00:03:48,882 --> 00:03:53,026
[SPEAKER_02]: I can bear a lot more, I cannot lose perspective, I can maintain my kindness in regard to others.

46
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:55,768
[SPEAKER_02]: What's the problem with a higher reference point of a higher self?

47
00:03:58,010 --> 00:03:58,711
[SPEAKER_02]: What's the issue?

48
00:03:59,171 --> 00:03:59,772
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there an issue?

49
00:04:03,873 --> 00:04:05,115
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it is, yeah, intoxicating.

50
00:04:05,155 --> 00:04:06,036
[SPEAKER_01]: It is very pleasurable.

51
00:04:06,096 --> 00:04:10,080
[SPEAKER_01]: You would see why that is very difficult to overcome that.

52
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:11,622
[SPEAKER_01]: But why would you overcome it if it's not an issue?

53
00:04:11,642 --> 00:04:13,144
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you wouldn't.

54
00:04:13,244 --> 00:04:14,946
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people don't.

55
00:04:15,146 --> 00:04:15,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

56
00:04:15,446 --> 00:04:17,448
[SPEAKER_02]: So, then, are you saying there is no issue with it?

57
00:04:17,889 --> 00:04:19,290
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean... Or there is an issue with it?

58
00:04:19,411 --> 00:04:20,171
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's what it is.

59
00:04:20,211 --> 00:04:22,034
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, from a personal point of view... Yeah.

60
00:04:22,614 --> 00:04:26,517
[SPEAKER_02]: Am I at risk, if I take that higher self?

61
00:04:27,178 --> 00:04:28,279
[SPEAKER_02]: Am I exposing myself?

62
00:04:28,479 --> 00:04:31,601
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, of course, because you can't discern the unknown ability of the self.

63
00:04:32,862 --> 00:04:36,105
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, unknown ability of it is the problem.

64
00:04:36,285 --> 00:04:36,885
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the issue.

65
00:04:37,506 --> 00:04:42,930
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the lack of discernment of the unknown ability.

66
00:04:43,431 --> 00:04:45,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the unknown ability is factual.

67
00:04:45,132 --> 00:04:48,214
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm just asking about the actual...

68
00:04:49,315 --> 00:04:51,817
[SPEAKER_02]: Property, say, of that experience.

69
00:04:52,118 --> 00:04:52,278
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

70
00:04:52,778 --> 00:05:01,506
[SPEAKER_02]: Whether you discern it or not, sure, that's again from the Buddhist point of view, but imagine somebody, a non-Buddhist person, what is an issue?

71
00:05:02,006 --> 00:05:03,748
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there an issue with a higher sense of self?

72
00:05:04,168 --> 00:05:08,412
[SPEAKER_02]: Without referring to, well, Buddha's teaching is better and free you from suffering.

73
00:05:08,432 --> 00:05:12,635
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I'm free from suffering when I believe, when I'm merged with my Atman or something.

74
00:05:12,755 --> 00:05:16,459
[SPEAKER_02]: So, from that point of view, whatever you're saying, it's already what I'm doing.

75
00:05:17,217 --> 00:05:18,938
[SPEAKER_02]: But then, is it so?

76
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:20,818
[SPEAKER_02]: Or it isn't?

77
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:25,280
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there an issue that whoever partakes in their view is not aware of?

78
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:31,422
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there an issue that whoever partakes in their view is... they're turning the blind eye towards... they're not seeing it, they're ignoring it.

79
00:05:32,182 --> 00:05:35,324
[SPEAKER_02]: So, yes, unknowability of it is an issue.

80
00:05:36,884 --> 00:05:41,726
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, see, you just assume it is your higher self, but

81
00:05:43,669 --> 00:05:49,370
[SPEAKER_02]: Do you know that that higher self is also not subjected to the same perturbing things?

82
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:49,730
[SPEAKER_02]: Sure.

83
00:05:50,430 --> 00:05:51,391
[SPEAKER_02]: It's on a higher level.

84
00:05:52,011 --> 00:05:54,971
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it does not get perturbed as easily as these other things.

85
00:05:55,051 --> 00:05:58,512
[SPEAKER_02]: But, ultimately, are you sure that it cannot be perturbed?

86
00:05:59,452 --> 00:06:01,993
[SPEAKER_02]: Are you sure that it cannot turn against you?

87
00:06:03,033 --> 00:06:04,733
[SPEAKER_02]: Are you sure that it cannot let you down?

88
00:06:05,394 --> 00:06:07,494
[SPEAKER_02]: Are you sure it will obey your will and save you?

89
00:06:08,583 --> 00:06:09,344
[SPEAKER_02]: How do you know that?

90
00:06:09,364 --> 00:06:10,425
[SPEAKER_02]: How do you know any of that?

91
00:06:10,945 --> 00:06:12,486
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you sure that it's forever?

92
00:06:12,727 --> 00:06:13,067
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

93
00:06:13,087 --> 00:06:13,988
[SPEAKER_02]: It boils down to that.

94
00:06:14,328 --> 00:06:20,213
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what he described in the suttas, the practices of other schools and teachings.

95
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:28,040
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, yes, some Samana and Brahmins would factually establish their mind upon the great element of earth, and they would abandon everything inferior to it.

96
00:06:29,061 --> 00:06:31,203
[SPEAKER_02]: But they would not understand the danger

97
00:06:32,171 --> 00:06:35,356
[SPEAKER_02]: of that element of earth that they have used to abandon everything inferior.

98
00:06:35,536 --> 00:06:37,038
[SPEAKER_02]: The target understands that as well.

99
00:06:37,499 --> 00:06:46,652
[SPEAKER_02]: They will not understand the danger, gratification, gratification, danger in the escape, in regard to earth, water, fire, ātman, consciousness, you know, Mūla Pāryāya's sutta, like the whole...

100
00:06:47,745 --> 00:06:50,906
[SPEAKER_02]: Seeing brahmas and everything, but conceiving them as yours.

101
00:06:51,627 --> 00:06:53,047
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's the root of the problem.

102
00:06:53,127 --> 00:06:56,249
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not that this sense of self is perturbed and you need to find a bigger one.

103
00:06:56,729 --> 00:06:59,590
[SPEAKER_02]: The reason is, whatever you find, you're going to conceive it as yours.

104
00:07:00,411 --> 00:07:03,232
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that is the the heart of the issue.

105
00:07:03,552 --> 00:07:08,694
[SPEAKER_02]: It's... it's even... even the most refined advaita experience, fundamentally, it's unownable.

106
00:07:08,874 --> 00:07:09,475
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not yours.

107
00:07:09,515 --> 00:07:12,176
[SPEAKER_02]: That's... there is no merging of yourself.

108
00:07:12,216 --> 00:07:16,818
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just basically refining the experience of exactly what Sācika said, of the five aggregates.

109
00:07:17,758 --> 00:07:20,540
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's, you know, in those other suttas, when the Buddha said, it doesn't matter.

110
00:07:21,601 --> 00:07:28,946
[SPEAKER_02]: If somebody claims, I'll show you the all apart from this all here, the five aggregates, six senses, there is no such thing.

111
00:07:29,226 --> 00:07:32,949
[SPEAKER_02]: He's contradicting himself, because there is nothing that he can show you that's outside of this.

112
00:07:33,810 --> 00:07:33,990
[SPEAKER_02]: So,

113
00:07:35,021 --> 00:07:44,685
[SPEAKER_02]: No matter how far you think you go, in your merging with your higher self, and it frees you from suffering and makes you forget about troubles of this life, that's still within this life.

114
00:07:45,205 --> 00:07:46,506
[SPEAKER_02]: That's still within these aggregates.

115
00:07:46,526 --> 00:07:48,106
[SPEAKER_02]: That's still subjected to these things.

116
00:07:49,987 --> 00:08:03,553
[SPEAKER_00]: The issue, then, is when that thing, which is subject to change, that higher self, whatever phenomenon you take as higher self, not seeing that it's dependent upon a lower self,

117
00:08:04,235 --> 00:08:05,075
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, yes, yeah.

118
00:08:05,316 --> 00:08:06,796
[SPEAKER_02]: That's like if you want to escape it.

119
00:08:06,836 --> 00:08:10,458
[SPEAKER_02]: But the real issue is simply you're not really addressing an issue.

120
00:08:11,559 --> 00:08:12,259
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the problem.

121
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:14,981
[SPEAKER_02]: You just replace one ownership for the other ownership.

122
00:08:15,541 --> 00:08:21,064
[SPEAKER_02]: Both things, because you conceive them as your... as... as ownable, that's why they're a problem.

123
00:08:21,104 --> 00:08:25,506
[SPEAKER_02]: See, the problem of the inferior self was not that he was perturbed.

124
00:08:26,446 --> 00:08:28,708
[SPEAKER_02]: The problem was that he was yours while he was perturbed.

125
00:08:30,389 --> 00:08:32,750
[SPEAKER_02]: So, then you realize perturbance cannot be stopped.

126
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:34,529
[SPEAKER_02]: But ownership can.

127
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:40,434
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you just slow down the perturbance, so to speak, by upgrading your higher sense of self.

128
00:08:40,474 --> 00:08:42,456
[SPEAKER_02]: But, fundamentally, you're still doing the same thing.

129
00:08:42,496 --> 00:08:43,296
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, still, I don't know.

130
00:08:43,316 --> 00:08:47,540
[SPEAKER_02]: You still... you haven't escaped the problem because of which you're doing what you're doing.

131
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:53,105
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the danger is still there, that you are... you are now taking something which is subject to change as yourself.

132
00:08:53,145 --> 00:08:53,365
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

133
00:08:53,385 --> 00:08:58,749
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're obviously subject to... and you might be quite comfortable in that

134
00:09:01,091 --> 00:09:11,196
[SPEAKER_00]: Taking that higher self as yourself, which seems permanent and so on, but at the end of the day, end of the life, you're going to get hit with... Chicken will come home to lose.

135
00:09:11,216 --> 00:09:13,377
[SPEAKER_00]: You're going to get slapped in the face with reality.

136
00:09:13,677 --> 00:09:20,860
[SPEAKER_00]: And how's that going to feel when you thought you had found something that was permanent and brings you... brought you safety, but now it's not.

137
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:22,941
[SPEAKER_00]: Why have you forsaken me, Lord?

138
00:09:23,081 --> 00:09:24,362
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

139
00:09:24,762 --> 00:09:25,503
[SPEAKER_00]: As Jesus said.

140
00:09:26,104 --> 00:09:34,651
[SPEAKER_02]: So, now, say somebody does recognize, okay, so, this higher sense of self, I couldn't regard it as not mine, equally.

141
00:09:35,131 --> 00:09:40,095
[SPEAKER_02]: In the same sense, I want to get rid of, overcome this perturbing self, sense of self that's constantly perturbed.

142
00:09:41,076 --> 00:09:43,718
[SPEAKER_02]: I could now have the same attitude towards this higher sense of self.

143
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:48,042
[SPEAKER_02]: So, how would they practically, what would they need to do?

144
00:09:49,423 --> 00:09:51,785
[SPEAKER_02]: Say, somebody does still have a view of the higher self,

145
00:09:53,269 --> 00:09:55,211
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't just stop thinking it, stop having it.

146
00:09:55,451 --> 00:09:56,652
[SPEAKER_02]: How do you free yourself from it?

147
00:09:57,734 --> 00:10:04,320
[SPEAKER_01]: So, while it's enduring, it's not trying to get rid of it, but see it as determined by...

148
00:10:05,644 --> 00:10:10,545
[SPEAKER_01]: That which is out of one's control, as the Buddha says in the Sutta, do you have control?

149
00:10:10,585 --> 00:10:12,886
[SPEAKER_01]: Like a king has control over his kingdom.

150
00:10:12,906 --> 00:10:15,767
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, this... Do you have control over matter or feeling?

151
00:10:16,147 --> 00:10:16,327
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

152
00:10:16,547 --> 00:10:18,208
[SPEAKER_02]: So, start pondering on its properties.

153
00:10:19,108 --> 00:10:20,268
[SPEAKER_02]: Of, like, well, do you have a saying?

154
00:10:20,288 --> 00:10:20,889
[SPEAKER_02]: It's arising.

155
00:10:21,129 --> 00:10:21,829
[SPEAKER_02]: How it arises?

156
00:10:22,249 --> 00:10:23,329
[SPEAKER_02]: Could you prevent it from leaving?

157
00:10:23,829 --> 00:10:24,290
[SPEAKER_02]: Do you know?

158
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:30,692
[SPEAKER_02]: Fundamentally, I think, the most practical thing would just come down to stop regarding it as your friend.

159
00:10:31,852 --> 00:10:35,413
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that's a completely gratuitous attitude that you just took.

160
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:36,720
[SPEAKER_02]: There's nothing.

161
00:10:37,201 --> 00:10:38,121
[SPEAKER_02]: They justified it.

162
00:10:40,903 --> 00:10:47,347
[SPEAKER_02]: But, automatically, people, when they find the higher self, it's automatically regarded as pleasurable mind.

163
00:10:47,667 --> 00:10:48,207
[SPEAKER_02]: It's my friend.

164
00:10:48,507 --> 00:10:49,268
[SPEAKER_02]: It's for my welfare.

165
00:10:49,288 --> 00:10:50,068
[SPEAKER_02]: It's for my being.

166
00:10:50,768 --> 00:10:57,172
[SPEAKER_02]: But, if you stop and think about it, there is no justification for that attitude, except you're taking it for granted, as such.

167
00:10:58,913 --> 00:11:00,314
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like... Why do you think it's your friend?

168
00:11:00,474 --> 00:11:05,377
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I guess it makes sense in the sense that it's... impermanence is like...

169
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:14,309
[SPEAKER_01]: It's less... in the sense that it changes at a slower rate than my smaller thing, which I'm more used to.

170
00:11:14,329 --> 00:11:16,591
[SPEAKER_02]: We don't need to figure out why you took it as friend.

171
00:11:17,492 --> 00:11:19,995
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to know why you're still holding it as friend.

172
00:11:20,015 --> 00:11:21,397
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what I meant to ask.

173
00:11:21,417 --> 00:11:25,682
[SPEAKER_02]: So, whichever way, one way or the other, you're gonna arrive at

174
00:11:27,511 --> 00:11:38,153
[SPEAKER_02]: Such experience of higher self, or meditation experience, or peace, or whatever, and you're going to regard it as friendly, as yours, as for you, as beneficial, as wholesome.

175
00:11:38,773 --> 00:11:40,194
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is that?

176
00:11:40,314 --> 00:11:45,195
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, why do you just not question that?

177
00:11:45,995 --> 00:11:47,895
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you have the sense of higher self.

178
00:11:48,655 --> 00:11:50,116
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't need to get rid of it.

179
00:11:50,176 --> 00:11:51,436
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't need to psychologize it.

180
00:11:51,476 --> 00:11:53,596
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't need to explain how it came to be.

181
00:11:54,216 --> 00:11:56,857
[SPEAKER_02]: You could just see it for what it is.

182
00:11:57,593 --> 00:12:02,515
[SPEAKER_02]: Fully take it, don't deny it, and then start regarding it as, but this is not my friend.

183
00:12:03,215 --> 00:12:06,877
[SPEAKER_02]: This is not mine, this is not for me, this is not for my welfare.

184
00:12:08,437 --> 00:12:18,101
[SPEAKER_02]: This is dangerous, this is a basically like that sutta says, you know, a friend, somebody who pretends to be a friend, just so that he can kill you, when you turn away.

185
00:12:19,282 --> 00:12:22,483
[SPEAKER_02]: You could choose to regard it that way, but that's the more unpleasant.

186
00:12:23,884 --> 00:12:26,865
[SPEAKER_02]: So, unless you have a good reason to do so, you naturally won't do so.

187
00:12:27,667 --> 00:12:30,429
[SPEAKER_02]: You would naturally just carry on regarding it as a friend.

188
00:12:30,490 --> 00:12:30,710
[SPEAKER_02]: Why?

189
00:12:31,010 --> 00:12:32,311
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that feels more pleasant.

190
00:12:33,092 --> 00:12:41,019
[SPEAKER_02]: So, fundamentally, chasing pleasure, avoiding pain, the reasons that your inferior self has been perturbed throughout this life,

191
00:12:42,109 --> 00:12:43,330
[SPEAKER_02]: That principle hasn't changed.

192
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:47,273
[SPEAKER_02]: You're still chasing pleasure, avoiding pain, just on a slower, higher rate.

193
00:12:47,793 --> 00:12:53,938
[SPEAKER_02]: But still doing the same thing, the same attitude, and that's why the same assumption of ownership, taking for granted, and everything else.

194
00:12:54,418 --> 00:12:55,179
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you haven't changed.

195
00:12:55,199 --> 00:12:57,360
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the problem of the higher self.

196
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:58,361
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not an escape.

197
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:00,743
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just another form of pleasure.

198
00:13:00,843 --> 00:13:03,485
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a perpetuation of the same principle.

199
00:13:03,585 --> 00:13:03,765
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

200
00:13:05,186 --> 00:13:05,826
[SPEAKER_00]: It takes... yeah.

201
00:13:07,888 --> 00:13:10,510
[SPEAKER_02]: So, yeah, have any mystical experience you want.

202
00:13:11,670 --> 00:13:27,986
[SPEAKER_02]: Any meditation release you want, and then regard it as an enemy, as a friend, as an enemy who pretends to be a friend, who wants to kill you, if you kind of, you know, turn away from it, and cultivate that attitude, and you will uproot any passion in regard to the world, and your meditation, and ātman, and everything else, and you'll be truly free.

203
00:13:28,727 --> 00:13:30,688
[SPEAKER_02]: You would understand gratification,

204
00:13:31,785 --> 00:13:44,516
[SPEAKER_02]: It's the light in it, the danger, oh, the peril, the trap, and then the escape, removal of gratification and desire towards it, in regard to the loftiest of the mystical experience that made you feel so special before.

205
00:13:45,496 --> 00:13:49,800
[SPEAKER_02]: And you'll be truly free, imperturbable, because nothing can be taken as mine now.

206
00:13:52,402 --> 00:13:55,545
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's giving up everything, basically.

207
00:13:55,585 --> 00:13:58,047
[SPEAKER_00]: Not taking anything as your self.

208
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:00,889
[SPEAKER_00]: Giving up ownership on any level.

209
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:06,003
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, and first you gotta, you gotta see where the problem is in the ownership.

210
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:11,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Without seeing it, you're just gonna be taking one thing instead of the other.

211
00:14:12,008 --> 00:14:13,809
[SPEAKER_02]: So that's that authenticity and transparency.

212
00:14:13,849 --> 00:14:22,475
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, now, whatever, whatever safety I've known, found, again, if you reflect upon it, you realize that you have no say in it.

213
00:14:22,595 --> 00:14:23,816
[SPEAKER_02]: Thus, you should not.

214
00:14:23,976 --> 00:14:26,398
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, you still can take it as your safety.

215
00:14:27,257 --> 00:14:34,259
[SPEAKER_02]: You still can remain regarding it as friendly, for me, pleasant, for my welfare.

216
00:14:35,439 --> 00:14:37,240
[SPEAKER_02]: But, if you're honest, you realize, well, I'm...

217
00:14:39,101 --> 00:14:47,803
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know that that is factually so, that this thing is factually friendly, yet I just choose to regard it because alternative feels more unpleasant.

218
00:14:48,363 --> 00:14:54,705
[SPEAKER_02]: So, thus, all I'm doing is acting away from pain towards pleasure, like what I always have been doing.

219
00:14:54,865 --> 00:14:56,706
[SPEAKER_02]: So, oh, that's why I'm unsafe.

220
00:14:57,821 --> 00:15:07,865
[SPEAKER_02]: Then a man truly wanting his own welfare will realize, no, I must abandon that, that ownership, that craving in regard to feeling, and then, then I'll deal with what's there left.

221
00:15:08,486 --> 00:15:11,707
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know what's gonna be, don't matter, but I know that this problem won't be there.

222
00:15:13,208 --> 00:15:23,352
[SPEAKER_02]: So you're not concerned then what's gonna happen after, you're just concerned removing what's here and now, that is an issue and the base for suffering.

223
00:15:25,293 --> 00:15:26,994
[SPEAKER_02]: And it is here and now, you know.

224
00:15:27,318 --> 00:15:27,958
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what Buddha said.

225
00:15:27,978 --> 00:15:32,941
[SPEAKER_02]: That's another famous passage that often gets mystified, like in the suttas.

226
00:15:33,361 --> 00:15:40,085
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, no, stop, you know, stop kind of going over the past and like, oh, what were you will be and what will be in the future.

227
00:15:41,206 --> 00:15:43,727
[SPEAKER_02]: Here, what's present, that's what you should abandon.

228
00:15:45,988 --> 00:15:48,970
[SPEAKER_02]: Here and now, that's what I'm abandoning, as in that's the root of the problem.

229
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:50,531
[SPEAKER_02]: I have refrained from...

230
00:15:51,507 --> 00:15:58,811
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, and then, and then, and this, and that, and that... Or, also, at the same time, I have refrained from... Well, in the past I did this, I did that... No, no, no.

231
00:15:59,011 --> 00:16:03,394
[SPEAKER_02]: Here and now is the issue in regard to craving, in regard to feeling, in regard to ownership, assumption.

232
00:16:03,794 --> 00:16:05,095
[SPEAKER_02]: And that is what I'm abandoning.

233
00:16:05,495 --> 00:16:08,037
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, past and future will even themselves out.

234
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,399
[SPEAKER_02]: But that, as I said, that gets mystified.

235
00:16:12,439 --> 00:16:15,501
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, oh, don't think about the past, don't plan the future, just be here now.

236
00:16:15,661 --> 00:16:16,361
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, no.

237
00:16:17,222 --> 00:16:19,123
[SPEAKER_02]: Just abandon your being here and now.

238
00:16:19,643 --> 00:16:20,204
[SPEAKER_02]: Understand it

239
00:16:22,975 --> 00:16:29,997
[SPEAKER_02]: Relinquish it, regard it as an enemy, not be here now, wow, look at this universal joy of this, this moment-to-moment experience.

240
00:16:31,038 --> 00:16:31,238
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

241
00:16:31,798 --> 00:16:33,058
[SPEAKER_02]: Sure, whatever you describe it.

242
00:16:34,599 --> 00:16:36,879
[SPEAKER_02]: The pure consciousness, my enemy.

243
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:42,301
[SPEAKER_02]: But this infinite awareness, phew, my threat, peril.

244
00:16:43,421 --> 00:16:48,823
[SPEAKER_02]: Here and now, body experience of this present moment, a trap.

245
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:58,533
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, there's no reason... Be here now and regard it as a trap every single second of your being there.

246
00:16:59,094 --> 00:16:59,635
[SPEAKER_02]: Rather than a...

247
00:17:00,272 --> 00:17:03,334
[SPEAKER_02]: Rather than you did the work already by being here now.

248
00:17:03,735 --> 00:17:11,421
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why I say all these other teachers and teachings and views, they kind of, they come up to, oh, be here now, that's the culmination.

249
00:17:11,441 --> 00:17:21,689
[SPEAKER_02]: You can have different permutations of where they come from and what do you do in account, what do you do in order to get there, but the culmination is present moment, here and now, that's it, that's it.

250
00:17:21,849 --> 00:17:22,349
[SPEAKER_00]: Celebrate.

251
00:17:22,809 --> 00:17:23,370
[SPEAKER_02]: That's it, yeah.

252
00:17:23,430 --> 00:17:25,552
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like, no, that's where dhamma actually starts.

253
00:17:26,172 --> 00:17:29,635
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, by all means, be here now and then start doing the work.

254
00:17:30,495 --> 00:17:34,996
[SPEAKER_02]: Of abandoning that here and now, through seeing the danger of it, the gratification, the peril.

255
00:17:36,336 --> 00:17:40,517
[SPEAKER_02]: And not just mystifying it and milking that experience more and more.

256
00:17:42,497 --> 00:17:46,718
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can't be here and now if you're intoxicated.

257
00:17:47,158 --> 00:17:47,338
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

258
00:17:48,238 --> 00:17:48,718
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

259
00:17:50,058 --> 00:17:53,879
[SPEAKER_02]: But then you also should not have a view that, oh, now I'm here and now my work's done.

260
00:17:54,599 --> 00:17:54,799
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

261
00:17:55,079 --> 00:17:58,740
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm here and now, let me find what work I need to do now.

262
00:18:00,459 --> 00:18:01,819
[SPEAKER_02]: How do I abandon this here and now?

263
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:07,381
[SPEAKER_02]: How do I prevent the possibility of intoxication arising, you know, in the future, by discerning?

264
00:18:07,481 --> 00:18:10,182
[SPEAKER_02]: How do I uproot my dependence on the pleasure of here and now?

265
00:18:12,162 --> 00:18:14,483
[SPEAKER_02]: How I remove any need for safety in here and now?

266
00:18:16,104 --> 00:18:19,385
[SPEAKER_02]: How I get my mind to turn away from here and now?

267
00:18:19,425 --> 00:18:19,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

268
00:18:21,125 --> 00:18:24,106
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, by contemplating danger in here and now, sufficiently.

269
00:18:25,485 --> 00:18:34,897
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the only way to get to see here and now, is to not distract yourself with sensual pleasures.

270
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:36,539
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

271
00:18:37,095 --> 00:18:41,976
[SPEAKER_02]: Because, as I said before, like, be here and now, as opposed to where?

272
00:18:42,356 --> 00:18:43,176
[SPEAKER_02]: Where else can you be?

273
00:18:43,276 --> 00:18:44,056
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

274
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:45,537
[SPEAKER_02]: Or stop thinking about the past.

275
00:18:45,577 --> 00:18:46,257
[SPEAKER_02]: Why?

276
00:18:46,277 --> 00:18:47,417
[SPEAKER_02]: You are doing that here and now.

277
00:18:47,977 --> 00:18:49,217
[SPEAKER_02]: Or don't plan about the future.

278
00:18:49,377 --> 00:18:50,138
[SPEAKER_02]: How is that possible?

279
00:18:50,698 --> 00:18:52,218
[SPEAKER_02]: And why would you not plan about... what?

280
00:18:52,558 --> 00:18:53,518
[SPEAKER_02]: You're doing it here and now.

281
00:18:54,118 --> 00:18:56,459
[SPEAKER_02]: If I think about the future, I'm doing it presently here and now.

282
00:18:56,979 --> 00:18:57,339
[SPEAKER_02]: What do you do?

283
00:18:57,379 --> 00:18:59,099
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm thinking, I'm just planning what you can do tomorrow.

284
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:00,100
[SPEAKER_02]: Here and now.

285
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:01,980
[SPEAKER_02]: So, why is that an issue?

286
00:19:04,812 --> 00:19:07,333
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can't leave here and now, even if you want to.

287
00:19:08,173 --> 00:19:11,034
[SPEAKER_02]: People want to leave here and now, when here and now is unpleasant.

288
00:19:11,394 --> 00:19:11,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I can.

289
00:19:12,314 --> 00:19:15,435
[SPEAKER_02]: But when here and now is pleasant, oh, then they want to mystify it.

290
00:19:16,415 --> 00:19:19,396
[SPEAKER_02]: But it's like... but it's still the same here and now.

291
00:19:19,416 --> 00:19:22,557
[SPEAKER_02]: As a framework of here and now, it's... it's still there.

292
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:25,040
[SPEAKER_02]: So, why do you want to leave it on some occasions?

293
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:26,701
[SPEAKER_02]: Why do you want to stop thinking about the past?

294
00:19:26,841 --> 00:19:28,541
[SPEAKER_02]: That's done here and now.

295
00:19:28,561 --> 00:19:29,902
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, because all this pain is coming up.

296
00:19:29,962 --> 00:19:32,462
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, so you just want to be here and now, when it's not unpleasant.

297
00:19:32,823 --> 00:19:37,124
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to be here and now, in order to avoid the pain of here and now.

298
00:19:38,764 --> 00:19:40,705
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's why it's not... it's never a resolution.

299
00:19:40,745 --> 00:19:42,425
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just perpetuation of the same issue.

300
00:19:46,166 --> 00:19:52,568
[SPEAKER_02]: So, first, yeah, you got to recognize that the only way to be here and now is not by intending to be here and now,

301
00:19:54,021 --> 00:19:57,045
[SPEAKER_02]: It's by not distracting yourself from here and now.

302
00:20:01,270 --> 00:20:03,473
[SPEAKER_02]: Not forgetting that you cannot not be here and now.

303
00:20:04,875 --> 00:20:06,898
[SPEAKER_02]: And you will forget that when you engage with your senses.

304
00:20:08,709 --> 00:20:11,992
[SPEAKER_02]: Mystical ideas, gratuitous ownerships and safeties and so on.

305
00:20:13,172 --> 00:20:15,094
[SPEAKER_00]: Just if you engage with craving.

306
00:20:15,434 --> 00:20:15,594
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

307
00:20:15,614 --> 00:20:16,675
[SPEAKER_00]: If you start acting out of craving.

308
00:20:16,695 --> 00:20:21,879
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you are... by acting out of craving, you're anticipating the future pleasure.

309
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:25,242
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're just in this anticipation, isn't it?

310
00:20:25,542 --> 00:20:26,483
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're not here and now.

311
00:20:26,603 --> 00:20:26,883
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

312
00:20:26,903 --> 00:20:27,523
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you are.

313
00:20:27,544 --> 00:20:28,284
[SPEAKER_00]: You are here and now.

314
00:20:28,364 --> 00:20:29,205
[SPEAKER_00]: But you completely...

315
00:20:29,425 --> 00:20:30,806
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't want to be here and now.

316
00:20:30,946 --> 00:20:32,047
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to be somewhere else.

317
00:20:32,067 --> 00:20:34,749
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to be here and now later on, when that here and now is pleasant.

318
00:20:34,949 --> 00:20:35,570
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

319
00:20:37,148 --> 00:20:38,589
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly, exactly.

320
00:20:38,609 --> 00:20:44,514
[SPEAKER_02]: The removal of craving means, like, there is no other option but to fully be here and now.

321
00:20:45,855 --> 00:20:47,216
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you are here and now.

322
00:20:48,537 --> 00:20:52,720
[SPEAKER_00]: So, don't worry, abandon the future.

323
00:20:53,261 --> 00:20:54,222
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't worry about the future.

324
00:20:55,603 --> 00:20:56,864
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't have anticipation.

325
00:20:57,244 --> 00:20:57,965
[SPEAKER_00]: Remove that anticipation.

326
00:20:57,985 --> 00:20:58,785
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, don't delight in it.

327
00:20:59,866 --> 00:21:00,426
[SPEAKER_00]: That craving.

328
00:21:00,447 --> 00:21:00,827
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

329
00:21:01,047 --> 00:21:02,288
[SPEAKER_02]: But you can't, like, I mean...

330
00:21:03,988 --> 00:21:07,751
[SPEAKER_02]: From here and now moment, next here and now moment, it's already me thinking about the future.

331
00:21:07,791 --> 00:21:08,131
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

332
00:21:08,411 --> 00:21:10,013
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you cannot think about the future.

333
00:21:10,053 --> 00:21:11,674
[SPEAKER_02]: Means, like, there will be being unconscious.

334
00:21:14,616 --> 00:21:19,420
[SPEAKER_02]: And same, if you can think about the future, means there will be... there is an implicit past carried with it.

335
00:21:20,441 --> 00:21:24,224
[SPEAKER_02]: Equally, it will mean you're unconscious, if you stop thinking about the past.

336
00:21:25,167 --> 00:21:26,989
[SPEAKER_02]: Just merge yourself in the present moment.

337
00:21:27,189 --> 00:21:30,111
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, why do you need to merge yourself with it when you're already in it?

338
00:21:30,452 --> 00:21:36,537
[SPEAKER_01]: So, now I have things about the future, things about the past, and... but the only difference is...

339
00:21:36,557 --> 00:21:37,618
[SPEAKER_02]: So, they are now here and now.

340
00:21:37,698 --> 00:21:38,439
[SPEAKER_02]: So, what's the difference?

341
00:21:38,899 --> 00:21:43,123
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, the difference is that that here and now feels unpleasant.

342
00:21:43,143 --> 00:21:46,766
[SPEAKER_02]: So, basically, I don't really care about here and now, or ātman for that matter, or anything else.

343
00:21:46,826 --> 00:21:49,569
[SPEAKER_02]: I just care about not feeling this discomfort and pain.

344
00:21:50,887 --> 00:21:51,927
[SPEAKER_02]: So, how do you deal with it?

345
00:21:51,967 --> 00:21:54,328
[SPEAKER_02]: By replacing it with pleasure, in an ignorant way.

346
00:21:54,848 --> 00:22:05,572
[SPEAKER_02]: If a person starts to, even though it doesn't matter, even if you're engaging in that, but you actually start honestly asking yourself certain questions, and you recognize that, okay, but the principle is still the same.

347
00:22:06,612 --> 00:22:13,555
[SPEAKER_02]: Here I am, claiming here and now is the way out, while here and now I'm trying to get rid of the here and now, that's not on my own terms.

348
00:22:13,575 --> 00:22:13,815
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

349
00:22:14,529 --> 00:22:16,810
[SPEAKER_02]: So, here and now, then, it's not the way out.

350
00:22:17,050 --> 00:22:20,312
[SPEAKER_02]: And it's not really even about here and now, or here and there, or whatever else.

351
00:22:20,372 --> 00:22:26,755
[SPEAKER_02]: It's about me getting rid of the pain when I'm touched by it, and me having pleasure or prolonging it when I'm touched by it.

352
00:22:26,815 --> 00:22:29,156
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's the root of the problem, that's the root of the unsafety.

353
00:22:29,196 --> 00:22:36,119
[SPEAKER_02]: So, how about... stop worrying about... yeah, stop worrying about past or future, or here and now, for that matter,

354
00:22:38,311 --> 00:22:45,796
[SPEAKER_02]: Undo your attitude towards pleasure and your attitude towards pain and your attitude towards neutral feeling.

355
00:22:45,936 --> 00:22:46,917
[SPEAKER_02]: That's all you need to do.

356
00:22:48,838 --> 00:22:49,939
[SPEAKER_02]: So, how do I start that?

357
00:22:49,959 --> 00:22:50,459
[SPEAKER_02]: What do I do?

358
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:52,381
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, come here, monk.

359
00:22:53,161 --> 00:22:54,722
[SPEAKER_02]: Dwell restrained by the precepts.

360
00:22:54,802 --> 00:22:55,623
[SPEAKER_02]: That's how you start.

361
00:22:56,635 --> 00:22:57,556
[SPEAKER_02]: And it will make sense.

362
00:22:57,736 --> 00:23:03,142
[SPEAKER_02]: If you want to uproot the craving in regard to your feeling, like if I feel pleasant, you want to remove the desire for more.

363
00:23:03,623 --> 00:23:07,267
[SPEAKER_02]: If you feel uncomfortable, you want to remove that aversion that trying to get rid of it.

364
00:23:07,788 --> 00:23:13,834
[SPEAKER_02]: And if you feel neutral, you want to remove that just distracted indolence of forgetting about yourself and drifting away.

365
00:23:14,675 --> 00:23:18,858
[SPEAKER_02]: So, first thing you do, well, okay, well, you gotta restrain your behavior by body.

366
00:23:18,918 --> 00:23:26,702
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't be engaging with these things that already depend on this craving in regard to your feeling, while expecting to remove the craving in regard to your feeling.

367
00:23:27,403 --> 00:23:30,485
[SPEAKER_02]: So, dwell restrained by the rules of patimokkha, so to say.

368
00:23:30,925 --> 00:23:32,226
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, guard the sense doors.

369
00:23:32,846 --> 00:23:34,087
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, be moderate in eating.

370
00:23:34,127 --> 00:23:37,569
[SPEAKER_02]: Basically, tone down, tame it, contain the behavior.

371
00:23:37,869 --> 00:23:41,972
[SPEAKER_02]: Don't let it keep spilling out on a various basis of craving.

372
00:23:43,382 --> 00:23:46,944
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, the mind and the here and now and everything else can become apparent.

373
00:23:46,984 --> 00:23:49,605
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, you could also exercise these attitudes towards it.

374
00:23:49,665 --> 00:23:54,428
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, so, this is perilous, this is not to be welcomed, this is not to be delighted in.

375
00:23:54,488 --> 00:23:55,288
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't need to get rid of it.

376
00:23:55,308 --> 00:23:56,089
[SPEAKER_02]: I can't get rid of it.

377
00:23:56,109 --> 00:23:58,130
[SPEAKER_02]: Getting rid of it would be another form of aversion of it.

378
00:23:58,190 --> 00:23:59,791
