00:34:41,802 --> 00:34:41,982
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

570
00:34:43,022 --> 00:34:44,843
[SPEAKER_02]: But the guarding of the sense door says it's not fine.

571
00:34:45,783 --> 00:34:47,764
[SPEAKER_02]: But the watchfulness of your intention says it's not fine.

572
00:34:48,224 --> 00:34:49,485
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you have a view now.

573
00:34:49,525 --> 00:34:50,465
[SPEAKER_02]: You have a choice to make.

574
00:34:51,612 --> 00:34:58,836
[SPEAKER_02]: Are you going to take the responsibility and use this internal criteria of greed, aversion, delusion, non-greed, non-aversion, delusion for the base of whether you should act or not?

575
00:34:59,297 --> 00:35:02,238
[SPEAKER_02]: Or are you going to go, well, yeah, but ājahn says, look, he does it, thus I can do it.

576
00:35:02,538 --> 00:35:04,099
[SPEAKER_02]: If it's fine for him, it's fine for me.

577
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:05,680
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's it.

578
00:35:05,780 --> 00:35:06,321
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, that person...

579
00:35:06,341 --> 00:35:07,821
[SPEAKER_02]: It means you're not taking it internally.

580
00:35:07,982 --> 00:35:10,203
[SPEAKER_02]: You're not, you have not taken even the precepts rightly.

581
00:35:11,604 --> 00:35:18,788
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's... the pull to to to continue acting is there, and there is still, um

582
00:35:20,820 --> 00:35:28,462
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, there's pressure and then, yeah, the choice to not act is where... Yeah, that's where the work is.

583
00:35:28,502 --> 00:35:46,026
[SPEAKER_02]: Which allows you to then discern craving, which allows you to... That's what I said, like, it's not, you know, understanding the dhamma, seeing the craving, it's not like, as I said, this hidden mystery and secret that you kind of have to, like, really, really discern and work hard intellectually to get to.

584
00:35:46,886 --> 00:35:49,467
[SPEAKER_02]: No, you have to work hard to withdraw yourself from where you are.

585
00:35:50,938 --> 00:35:56,983
[SPEAKER_02]: You draw the mind from the senses, from the dependence on the pleasure of the senses, from acting out of pressure, and then you'll see it.

586
00:35:57,123 --> 00:35:57,564
[SPEAKER_01]: It's right there.

587
00:35:57,584 --> 00:35:58,604
[SPEAKER_01]: It's gonna be right there in your face.

588
00:35:59,125 --> 00:35:59,765
[SPEAKER_01]: Very tangible.

589
00:36:00,026 --> 00:36:00,206
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

590
00:36:00,246 --> 00:36:00,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

591
00:36:01,247 --> 00:36:03,028
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's the difficult part.

592
00:36:03,108 --> 00:36:04,649
[SPEAKER_02]: It's exactly what nobody wants to do.

593
00:36:04,669 --> 00:36:14,718
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, people can sit for hours and ponder on dhamma, and figure it out, and read the dictionaries, and get the degrees in it, and know every single text, and... Loads of effort, I mean, factually.

594
00:36:14,958 --> 00:36:17,360
[SPEAKER_02]: Loads of effort, and time, and discomfort.

595
00:36:18,481 --> 00:36:19,662
[SPEAKER_02]: But what they don't want to do

596
00:36:20,169 --> 00:36:37,458
[SPEAKER_02]: He's endured the pressure on the level of feeling and not act out of it, not get rid of it, not try to justify it, not to psychologize it, not explain it, just endured it, without distracting yourself from it, without falling back onto the senses to cover it up.

597
00:36:39,559 --> 00:36:41,560
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the... yeah, that's the middle way.

598
00:36:41,860 --> 00:36:42,380
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, the only way.

599
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:43,120
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why it's not done.

600
00:36:44,041 --> 00:36:46,382
[SPEAKER_02]: Because it's the subtlest one to see and stick with it.

601
00:36:49,697 --> 00:36:57,099
[SPEAKER_02]: But if somebody is diligent in that regard, then, yeah, you don't even have to worry about the craving and paticcaṁpāda and everything else.

602
00:36:58,699 --> 00:36:59,600
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just going to be seen there.

603
00:37:01,060 --> 00:37:02,260
[SPEAKER_01]: Very real.

604
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:02,881
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

605
00:37:03,001 --> 00:37:04,221
[SPEAKER_02]: And also where it is.

606
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:14,404
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, see, when you're trying to think about it before you have developed your behavior, your mind, withdrawn from sensuality, that which you think craving is, isn't.

607
00:37:15,364 --> 00:37:17,184
[SPEAKER_02]: That which you think your aggregates are, aren't.

608
